# PLAYER PROFILE with every slot Empty (121939-profile-select.png). The
# returning route's A then opened the name keyboard, its stick pulse moved
# the cursor N -> O, and `mark gameplay` landed on that keyboard
# (122018-gameplay.png). The 1200 s confirmation and session 40's
# benchmark (100% at 59.94) both measured that menu, not a race.
# A single route runs whatever titlestate believes the disk holds.
#
# Its assumption: the soak's disk has NO 187 profile (true of every soak so
# far; the route never flushes, so it does not leave one behind). If a disk
# ever does hold profile "N", the first A loads it and the rest of the route
# misses the menus; the frames show it at profile-select.
#
# Boot with no input (scratch/replay/bootwatch-191916): Ubisoft and ESRB
# 6-16 s, "Please press START to begin" from ~22 s to ~50 s after launch,
# then an attract race with a full HUD (NOT gameplay: nobody is driving).
# One START in that window, held 150 ms (a 60 ms START was missed once).
#
# Empty profile list: A (Create) opens a name keyboard with "N" highlighted;
# A enters it and Y validates, which goes straight to the main menu (a
# horizontal list: Story mode, Quick hits, Xbox Live, ...). One left-stick
# pulse moves one item. Quick hits -> Western Whip Race -> Buck -> the sport
# car. A new profile's first race shows Controller Configuration (Classic);
# A accepts it. Then a narrated tutorial clip that drives itself ("To
# accelerate big dog style..."): A skips it (START does not). The race
# (lap 1/4, 6 cars) starts ~8 s after the skip.
#
# Player control (session 37 nav frames 045-048): the left stick steered the
# car into a tanker (44 -> 22 mph), holding A (Classic: accelerate) took it
# back to 37. The mark is placed after 6 s of that input, in the race.
#
# One boot in three in session 37 hung on a black spinner at 3 fps
# (hakuX-watchdog STALL, eip=0x800151ed, IF=0), the first boot after a
# flush. It did not recur on the next launch.
wait 5.0
shot boot
